                    </mxGeometry>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="3tbVxYwfYqRhcP25RS5C-7" value="Problem: for auditing to execute succesfully someone needs to upload/present AuditingData. If someone presents junk AuditingData the check dispute.auditingDataHash == hash(auditingData) will FAIL -&amp;gt; in the current model any failure in auditing will result in slashing the disputer, so the check dispute.auditingDataHash == hash(auditingData) hash to be done on the outside (in the challenge)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In the case that the disputer committed to some junk auditingDataHash -&amp;gt; we can prove that with a DisputeFraudProof by actually presenting the correct AuditingData (verification gcode explained above) and proving that hash(correct AuditingData) != dispute.auditingDataHash" style="text;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;overflow=hidden;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;rotatable=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="3tbVxYwfYqRhcP25RS5C-6" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry y="30" width="500" height="170" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="3tbVxYwfYqRhcP25RS5C-9" value="The current auditing code can be split into small DisputeFraudProofs and checked 1 by 1 in isolation and what we call auditing can be &quot;Run all DisputeFraudProofs&quot; and is some are succesfull trigger them on-chain." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="MiHG-ok4c3-oJHMUXmo7-8" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="100" y="80" width="370" height="210" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
